From 4fbf6289e3736a9f34c5fe444e1c7cdab8547ce1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:56:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a placement requeue is never refused for quoted
 text, nor run here when it fails [daveey]

A hub refusal or exception quoted in a placement requeue's reason/why can read like an agent wall
("permission denied", "waiting for Owner"): the declared clock's text_wall check refused the park, main()'s
retry raised again, and main() fell back to running the worker locally, even for a qualified-origin card.

- kanban_awaiting.resolve(system=True), passed by gate(count_repeats=True): a system clock re-park skips the
  agent-prose checks (text_wall, soak_wait); it still needs its why. Narrower than rewording every requeue
  text, and the quoted hub text stays visible on the card.
- kanban_placement_forward.recover/hold: when a forward step and its requeue both raise, a sent or
  qualified-origin card (or one whose state is unreadable) is blocked transient with the error, never exec'd
  here; only an unsent card with a local fallback still falls back.
- Tests: the wall text through the not-live, refused-no-fallback and step-failed requeues; main() holds a
  qualified-origin and a sent card; an unsent local card still falls back (red without the fix).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
